[2026-09-25T18:35:10.441Z] The unit files have no installation config (WantedBy=, RequiredBy=, UpheldBy=,
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.441Z] Also=, or Alias= settings in the [Install] section, and DefaultInstance= for
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.441Z] template units). This means they are not meant to be enabled or disabled using systemctl.
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.441Z]  
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.441Z] Possible reasons for having these kinds of units are:
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.441Z] • A unit may be statically enabled by being symlinked from another unit's
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.441Z]   .wants/, .requires/, or .upholds/ directory.
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.442Z] • A unit's purpose may be to act as a helper for some other unit which has
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.442Z]   a requirement dependency on it.
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.442Z] • A unit may be started when needed via activation (socket, path, timer,
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.442Z]   D-Bus, udev, scripted systemctl call, ...).
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.442Z] • In case of template units, the unit is meant to be enabled with some
[2026-09-25T18:35:10.442Z]   instance name specified.
